      <h2>About</h2>
      <p>Jonas Rech is an independent web and brand designer based in Brno, Czech Republic.</p>
      <p>He helps businesses improve how they present themselves through clear communication, strong visual identity and modern websites.</p>
      <p>His work combines web design, UX/UI, brand identity, development, copy and photography. He works directly with clients from the initial direction and structure through visual design and final implementation.</p>
      <p>Rather than treating design and development as separate parts of the process, Jonas combines them to create websites that feel consistent from the first idea to the final product.</p>
      <p>He works primarily with businesses, founders and smaller teams in the Czech Republic and internationally.</p>

      <h2>Services &amp; expertise</h2>
      <h3>Web design &amp; development</h3>
      <p>Design and development of modern websites with a focus on clear structure, typography, usability, responsive design and visual detail.</p>
      <p>Typical work includes:</p>
      <ul><li>company websites</li><li>website redesigns</li><li>landing pages</li><li>UX/UI design</li><li>responsive web design</li><li>interaction and motion design</li><li>frontend development</li><li>CMS implementation</li></ul>
      <h3>Brand identity</h3>
      <p>Visual direction and identity for businesses that need a clearer and more consistent way to present themselves.</p>
      <p>This can include:</p>
      <ul><li>visual identity</li><li>typography</li><li>color systems</li><li>art direction</li><li>brand direction</li><li>digital brand systems</li></ul>
      <h3>Content &amp; photography</h3>
      <p>When appropriate, Jonas also works with website copy and original photography so that content, imagery and design share the same visual direction.</p>

      <h2>Approach</h2>
      <p>Jonas starts with understanding the business before designing the website.</p>
      <p>The goal is to understand what the business does, what makes it different, who it needs to reach and what the website needs to communicate.</p>
      <p>His design approach is generally:</p>
      <ul><li>contemporary</li><li>typography-led</li><li>minimal</li><li>editorial</li><li>structured</li><li>detail-oriented</li><li>motion-aware</li><li>photography-conscious</li></ul>
      <p>He prefers clear communication and strong visual hierarchy over unnecessary complexity or generic design trends.</p>

      <h2>Tools &amp; technology</h2>
      <p><strong>Design:</strong> Figma · Affinity · Adobe Photoshop · Adobe Lightroom</p>
      <p><strong>Development:</strong> Astro · React · Next.js · TypeScript · Tailwind CSS · Sanity CMS · Vercel</p>
      <p><strong>Platforms:</strong> Framer</p>
      <p>Jonas also uses AI-assisted tools for research, prototyping and development where they make the process faster or more effective. Creative direction and final design decisions remain human-led.</p>

